         <head>THE SOCIAL LADDER</head>
         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>The Social Ladder / Drawings by Charles Dana Gibson</head>
            <lg>
               <l>
                  <hi rend="italic">Drawings by</hi>
               </l>
               <l/>
               <l>CHARLES DANA GIBSON</l>
               <l/>
               <l/>
               <l/>
               <l>
                  <hi rend="italic">New York</hi>: R. H. RUSSELL <hi rend="italic">London</hi>: JOHN LANE 1902</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">  This is the seventh book in the regular series of Mr. Gibson’s published drawings, consisting of:</p>
            <table rend="frame" xml:id="Table2">
               <row>
                  <cell>DRAWINGS BY C. D. GIBSON</cell>
                  <cell>No. 1</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>PICTURES OF PEOPLE</cell>
                  <cell>No. 2</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>SKETCHES AND CARTOONS</cell>
                  <cell>No. 3</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>THE EDUCATION OF MR. PIPP</cell>
                  <cell>No. 4</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>AMERICANS</cell>
                  <cell>No. 5</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>A WIDOW AND HER FRIENDS</cell>
                  <cell>No. 6</cell>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <cell>THE SOCIAL LADDER</cell>
                  <cell>No. 7</cell>
               </row>
            </table>
            <p rend="justify">Each book contains eighty-four of Mr. Gibson’s best cartoons, and all are uniform in size, shape and binding. Thanks are due Messrs. Mitchell &amp; Miller for their co-operation in making this volume as representative and complete as possible.</p>
            <lg>
               <l>Copyright by Mitchell &amp; Miller</l>
               <l>COPYRIGHT, 1902, BY ROBERT HOWARD RUSSELL</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">THIS book is published in Great Britain by especial arrangement with Mr. James Henderson, the proprietor of the English copyright of some of the drawings.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Printed in the United States of America, in July, 1902<lb/>Entered at Stationers’ Hall</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE SOCIAL LADDER</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">An Imitation of the lady of the house.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">MRS. STEELE POOLE’S HOUSEWARMING.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">She</hi>: “You don’t know what it is to love.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">“I don’t, eh? Haven’t I been to every play, read every popular novel in the last six months, got into debt hopelessly, had my appendix removed, and all for your sake?”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">Mr. Meeker doesn’t object so much to his wife’s entertainments as he does to the way she uses his room for the gentlemen’s things.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">HIS REVENGE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Time: Any morning at 4:15.</hi>
            </p>
            <p rend="justify">Mr. Meeker, having been kept up late for the last twenty years and rebuked for his lack of interest, develops a sudden enthusiasm. Mrs. Meeker and the girls now do the waiting.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">At a dramatic agency.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE SONG OF THE DÉBUTANTE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">“Mother, dear Mother, come home with me now.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE TROUBLES OF THE RICH.</p>
            <p rend="justify">At the last moment, several who were invited send their regrets.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE STORY OF HIS LIFE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE HEIRESS.</p>
            <lg>
               <l>She cannot talk, she cannot sing,</l>
               <l>  She looks a fright; but folks aver</l>
               <l>  Ten millions have been set apart</l>
               <l>  To talk and sing and look for her.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">Mr. Grubbs walks in his sleep and appears for the first and only time at an entertainment in his own house.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">WHY NOT</p>
            <p rend="justify">have plate glass fronts to the opera boxes? The occupants could still be seen, but not heard.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE NEXT MORNING</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Mrs. Innittor Dedd’s maid reads</hi>: “Among those present was Mrs. Innittor Dedd, whose lovely face and splendid figure were enhanced by a tiara of diamonds and three ropes of pearls. She wore her famous rubies and was even more regal than at the Bullyon’s ball the night before,” ETC., ETC.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">ADVICE TO A HOSTESS.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Keep your entertainment within the mental grasp of your guests.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">MODERN CELEBRITIES.</p>
            <p rend="justify">An interesting discussion between the author of “The Barrenness of Unkissed Kisses” and a famous dramatist.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">WASTED ENERGY.</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Professor Bung</hi>: A beauty? Well, perhaps she is.</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">Mr. Rattles</hi>: Why, man, haven’t you noticed the divine way she smiles?</p>
            <p rend="justify">“Oh, I’m not altogether unobservant. I have made a calculation, in fact, that the energy expended on her smiles, if scientifically applied, would run an automobile.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Showing that a man may be a hero in his own house.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">PARASITES.</p>
            <p rend="justify">Basking in the golden sunshine.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">OF COURSE THERE ARE MERMAIDS.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">PLENTY OF GOOD FISH IN THE SEA.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">HIS CHRISTMAS GIFT.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">A SUGGESTION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">For ill-assorted pairs.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">Mrs. Katcham prides herself on always having the latest celebrity at her house. To-night it is no less a personage than “Gouger.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">While Uncle Joe has his tie fixed.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">A CROOKED TALE.</p>
            <lg>
               <l>There was a crooked man,</l>
               <l>  Who made a crooked deal,</l>
               <l>  And got a crooked fortune</l>
               <l>  By a very crooked steal;</l>
               <l>  He had a crooked wife,</l>
               <l>  With a very crooked name,</l>
               <l>  And now they live apart</l>
               <l>  In very crooked fame.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">He</hi>: You promised to be my pupil and learn to love me.</p>
            <p rend="justify">“But it makes such a difference when your heart isn’t in your work.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE AMBITIOUS MOTHER AND THE OBLIGING CLERGYMAN.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">FROZEN.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">WHERE IGNORANCE, ETC.</p>
            <p rend="justify">“Where did you go on your wedding trip?”</p>
            <p rend="justify">“That’s what I’ve been wondering.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">While a Spanish-American hero describes the horrors of war.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE MERRY-GO-ROUND.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE BROKER RINGS UP HIS GIRL.</p>
            <p rend="justify">“Hello! Hello! Big strike in Consolidated Catamount—can marry—want three days’ option hand and heart.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">
               <hi rend="italic">She</hi>: Will give refusal.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">ANOTHER MOTH.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE ENTHUSIAST WHO INSISTS UPON SHOWING YOU HIS ESTATE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDY IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">While the hostess whispers to Jones, “Remember, now, we are counting on you to make us laugh.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify"> </p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">ONE OF THE DISADVANTAGES OF BEING IN LOVE WITH AN ATHLETIC GIRL.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">Pillsbury does not care for society, but his wife will not go without him.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">WHY SOME CHILDREN DIDN’T GET THEIR PRESENTS.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">ALAS! THE VOICE OF HIS FIANCÉE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">STUDIES IN EXPRESSION.</p>
            <p rend="justify">The author and the soubrette.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">THE HALF ORPHAN.</p>
            <p rend="justify">“Mamma will be down in a minute.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">“UNLUCKY AT CARDS, LUCKY IN LOVE.”</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
            <p rend="justify">WHEN A MAN’S IN LOVE.</p>
            <p rend="justify">[Image unavailable.]</p>
